  "reason": "The current best (config_026: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.635) has been validated across profile setting, aggregation, and fusion choices, but the image encoder dimension remains entirely untested—every completed experiment used imagenet_vit_l. config_007 swaps only the image encoder to resnet50 while holding all other settings identical to config_026, giving a clean single-variable A/B comparison. This is the highest-value next experiment because: (1) image-only performance was very low (0.227), so it's unclear how much the specific image encoder matters in the multimodal context; (2) if resnet50 performs comparably, the image encoder choice is a low-priority design decision and we can focus budget on RNA encoder variants (e.g., scvi_n200); if it degrades significantly, we confirm imagenet_vit_l is essential and should not be swapped. This single experiment resolves a major source of uncertainty across the entire multimodal design space under the limited budget."
}

